# VPSie Provider

The VPSie provider is used to manage resources on the
[VPSie](https://vpsie.com) cloud platform with Terraform or OpenTofu. Use it to
provision and manage servers, block and object storage, networking (VPCs,
firewalls, floating IPs, gateways, load balancers), DNS, TLS certificates,
Kubernetes clusters, container registries, managed databases, tags and more.

## Authentication

The provider needs a VPSie API access token. Set it with the `access_token`
argument or, preferably, the `VPSIE_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable so the
token never ends up in configuration or state:

```shell
export VPSIE_ACCESS_TOKEN="your-api-token"
```

Issue a token from the VPSie console under API access.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/provider/provider.tf" }}

```terraform
resource "vpsie_server_group" "web" {
  group_name        = "web-tier"
  group_description = "Front-end web servers"
  is_distributed    = true
}
```

